                "quote": "The easiest way to use orbital and auxiliary basis sets in ORCA is via the simple input keywords. All available orbital basis set keywords can be found in Section 2.7.2 and all auxiliary basis set options in Section 2.7.4. For example, the Karlsruhe def2-TZVP basis set can be invoked via the def2-TZVP keyword.\n\ndef2-TZVP H–Rn def2-ECP (Rb–Rn) Polarized valence triple-\\(\\zeta\\). Quite similar to the older def-TZVPP for main group elements and TZVP for H."
